    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, keeping the given signature. It validates inputs and raises `ValueError` for unknown regions or categories, bad `qty` (including `bool`), negative prices or credit, and discounts outside 0–100. Line net applies the line discount, then the 5% bulk discount for `standard` lines with `qty` ≥ 10, and rounds to cents. Tax is computed per line from the rounded net, with all rounding `ROUND_HALF_UP` to 2 places. Totals, credit handling and `tax_by_rate` (including 0% rates that appear on a line) are derived from those per-line values. I wrote 24 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py` covering the rules, rounding edge cases, credit cases and invalid inputs. One test I first wrote had a wrong expected net (I summed to 50 instead of 40); I corrected the test, not the implementation. `python -m pytest -q tests` now passes all 24 tests.",
